        "problem": "Express $\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(x+{225}^{\u2218})$ in terms of $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x.$\n\n$\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(x+{225}^{\u2218})=$\n{{field-1}}$\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\,-$\n{{field-2}}$\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x$",
        "worked_solution": "First, we recall the sum formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(u+v)=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061u\\operatorname{cos}\u2061v-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061u\\operatorname{sin}\u2061v\n$$\n\nApplying the sum formula for cosine with $u=x$ and $v={225}^{\u2218}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(x+{225}^{\u2218}) & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{225}^{\u2218}-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061{225}^{\u2218} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
